    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75807" body-key="">
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἄρα,</span></b> 
		Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>so not, not then</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἄρα σοί γε πατὴρ ἦν . . Πηλεύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.33
				</span></i>
			. </div>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in questions, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἄρ᾽ ἔμελλες οὐδὲ θανὼν λήσεσθαι . .
				χόλου</span><i>; so not</i> even in death wert thou to
			forget thine anger? <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.553
			</span></i>.</div>
	</div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
